The runtime package is named FirstClass2000_vcl4.bpl for Delphi4/Builder4, and FirstClass2000_vcl5.bpl for Delphi 5/Builder 5. You will need to distribute the appropriate file if you are compiling your project with the 1stClass runtime package.  You shoul
d also update your project's .dpr, .bpr, .mak files so that they refer to the new package names and libraries.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {
\par }{\b Installing the 1stClass help files \endash  }{You will need to run the OpenHelp utility by clicking on Help | Customize from the Delphi or Builder IDE.  F
rom there, click on Edit | Add Files to add the appropriate 1stClass help file: 1stclass_d4.hlp (Delphi 4), 1stclass_d5.hlp (Delphi 5), 1stclass_c4.hlp (C++ Builder 4), or 1stclass_c5.hlp (C++ Builder 4). You should add the file to the list of help files 
in the index and link tab pages. Do not add it to the contents tab page. After adding the .hlp file, click on }{\i File}{ | }{\i Save Project }{to save your changes.
\par 
\par }{\i Warning}{ \endash  Delphi 5's default help indexing is near the limits of Microsoft's WinHelp.  As a result, you 
may need to remove any indexes you do not regularly use do stay within the capabilities of WinHelp.  If you experience an empty list on the Index tab page of WinHelp, this indicates you need to remove some .hlp files using OpenHelp.
\par 
